G'day all,

        I have been playing Hack and NetHack for the best part of a year now
(the worst part being that I also had to finish an honours degree), and I have a
few suggestions to the dev. team;

        1. I LOVE the idea of a wall mirror. The idea of attacking yourself for
double the stuff that you already have is a great one. Some more improvements
though;
    a/ You alter-ego will have the "opposite" named weapon to you eg. you have
Stormy, he has Excalibur, you have Cleaver he has Snikersnee, you have
Frostbrand, he has Firebrand etc.
    b/ Rather than giving him -3 objects where you have +3 objects, give him
cursed where you have blessed etc. (=> a blessed lodestone would have some use,
as you could drop it, but he couldn't, and would collapse under his load).
    c/ If you apply your mirror to the wall mirror, the room could fill up with
your alter-egos, and you would be history.
    d/ If you enter the room with a blindfold on, you could stand in front of
the mirror, and you could get the message "You sense a familliar presence
nearby...".
    e/ Mirrors are a once-off thing, otherwise you could use it to get multiple
wands of wishing (have one the first time, two the next etc..).

        2. How about a level out in a forrest? The level could consist of lots
of trees, and every now and again, there could be an Ent (see Tolkien) which is
like a Mimic, in that you could detect it with your blindfold but not see it (it
just looks like a tree). Ents could be made very tough, and if one attacks you
the others on the level could come to help it out (big troubles if you don't
have a ring of conflict). In this case, the axe named Cleaver could be made a
far superior weapon to the others, and fight these Ents very well. You could
also have a clearing in the trees where there is a pool of water. Somewhere
nearby there could be a Bunyip ('cause I'm an Aussie and we get a lot of them
'round here). A Bunyip could be about as tough as a Jabberwock. The pool may
even be given magic properties of some sort (ie worth the trouble of disposing
of Ents and the Bunyip), e.g. tell you which level the Wiz is on(?)

        Anyway, these are just a couple of ideas, what do other people think
about them?


